ich people completely lost all  control and they turn into flesh-eating  monsters intent on ripping you apart as  the military and government learn more  about the virus we discover that it  actually completely kills the carrier  and just stimulates their body basically  making their corpse move the variant to  this is 98 similar but the host retains  their consciousness and thus we get a  human zombie hybrid that appears fine  from the outside but they do hunger for  human flesh from time to time the idea  of a virus is laced throughout the show  and even in the title sequence we see  several of the undead laid out in a way  that's similar to how the disease is  shown in episode 9. like most korean  shows there's a lot of social commentary  and throughout the season we see vast  blankets of the public believing that  the outbreak is fake news we watch  quarantine zones being set up and even  get bullying metaphors laced throughout  the entire thing the latter of these  comes in the form of guinem a guy that  should have been killed for the mullet  alone in the series he ends up becoming  infected with the mutated version of the  virus and he attempts to track down his  bitter school rival chong san and the  other students that he's with among  cesar suyuk the leader that everyone  wishes they were in school namra the  class president that should be president  of the world on joe whose dad's a  firefighter desperately looking for her  and several others most of which get  picked off one by one queen am is  basically like the nemesis from resident  evil with a mullet and he stalks the  corridors looking for the group  desperate for revenge no matter how many  times they defeat him he always comes  back and during the series namra gets  infected with the same mutation that he  has this grants her increased strength  and power but like the rest of the  undead she too starts to yearn for human  flesh in the subplot the military  realized that the undead can be herded  by using the frequency of 24 kilohertz  and thus they put together a plan to  usher all of the zombies into a specific  area with drones they'll bomb the living  sorry dying hell out of them and  basically try and contain the virus as  much as possible this is inspired by the  final video left by the science teacher  in which he realizes that the only way  to destroy the virus is to wipe it out  completely obviously there wouldn't be  much tension if the school wasn't one of  the locations getting bombed and thus  there becomes somewhat of a race to get  out of dodge before school's out  [Music]  [Applause]  forever now towards the end of the  season the group raced to a construction  site right beside the school and it's at  this point that they're attacked by  guinam chung-sang gets bit and thus he  remains behind to buy this time in order  to escape the battle is as bloody as  you'd expect and it really sums up the  phrase an eye for an eye as they battle  it out the missiles start to bombard the  area and chung sign ends up taking  guinham down a half built elevator shaft  where the two both perish now i have  seen people online going back and forth  over whether cheong sang is actually  dead and i'm unsure too due to the  evidence that we get the first of which  comes when the pair both go down the  elevator shaft and we only see guinea's  body being obliterated in the fire i've  slowed down the footage so you can see  this happening but chiang sang does get  engulfed by it too however he doesn't  really get the orangey burn that guinam  does and his head can also still be seen  occurred at the end of the episode when  we close in on on joe's name badge and  you can also see a set of fingers  possibly belonging to the character  however in episode 12 we do see what  looks like his body along with several  others personally i think that the  character is likely dead but there are  several times throughout the season  where they imply that he's finished and  the next episode we learn that isn't the  case when looking for him namra says  that she can't smell anything which is a  line that is stuck in my head long after  finishing the season i think this could  have been done on purpose to give the  audience the idea that he might have  actually survived the encounter it's  pretty crazy if he did but at the end of  the season we do get lip service paid  towards other characters being out there  now this isn't me confirming whether  he's alive or not and in all honesty  like i said i'm not that sure myself i  think it does leave an opening for the  creative team to potentially bring him  back but the bombing itself was extreme  so if he doesn't return then at least he  went out with a bang  [Music]  now this causes so much pain that the  head of the military actually ends his  own life and it definitely feels like  this is a series that doesn't really  have any winners this is reflected in  several of the parents that die in order  to save their kids most notably on joe's  father nam soju now throughout the  series he makes a daring journey out of  the quarantined zone in order to save  his daughter just as he's reunited with  her he ends up sacrificing himself in  order to save her from being eaten by  zombies it's a pretty devastating gut  punch but he doesn't die in vain as when  the students finally escape the school  they find ribbons amongst the trees that  lead them somewhat to safety eventually  the group make it to young dung but  they're not out of the woods yet and we  get one final death in woojin a kid who  saves his badass sister with a bow she's  so cool isn't she she she is cool to be  fair now jin ends up turning but  unfortunately his sister can't bring  herself to kill him and thus namra steps  in in order to break his neck this sets  off hari but it also causes urges within  namra to feed on her flesh anjo even  offers herself up as a meal but namra  decides to stay in control and then she  makes a choice to remain behind whilst  the group go into the quarantine zone  eventually they make it but they're put  in prison and interrogated over what  they know of the events they've been  through hell which has really matured  them and in the end they stand up for  themselves and refuse to cooperate this  was a government that left them behind  to die on the off chance that they were  infected and thus they stand firm in  their stents over time as the virus dies  down things start to open up once more  and we get a time jump of four months in  which the group are finally freed this  is along with several of the other  characters that we met throughout the  series who somewhat get a happy ending  as a precaution though the residents of  the area are kept in quarantine whilst  career and the rest of the world come to  grips with what happened people have had  their homes and lives destroyed over  something that could have been prevented  had more care being given at a human  level now in the aftermath we follow on  joe as she sneaks out of the compound  one night and during this journey she  notices a fire on the school roof namra  said that if they ever met again that  they should have a campfire and after  telling su yuk the rest of the survivors  go back into the restricted zone  searching for their friend  upon huddling together on the roof they  come across namra and it's a pretty  pretty pretty heartfelt reunion now it  brings everything together and though  the groups still refer to her as their  prez they know that they can't be  together namra says that she's neither  human or a monster and though they want  her to stay with them she says that  she's found a new purpose now the series  is very much a coming-of-age story in  which our characters mature and grow as  people namra says that it's sort of like  being between a child and an adult which  is of course reflected in the teenagers  themselves anja at one point even says  that she'll never help adults again and  in some ways the group are something new  themselves much like the hybrids they've  seen the ugly side of society and though  they will live among it it's unlikely  that they'll ever truly feel part of it  again namra says that she wants to help  the others like her that have been  forced to live in restricted zones and  she leaps off into the night sky and  probably a second season  it's been trending all weekend now going  forward i do think that we will probably  follow namra on the most part as she  starts to survey the area i think that  most of the characters will return to  somewhat normality after their feed from  quarantine but with the virus still  being out there there is the possibility  that it could spread once more like all  humans the hybrids will have their own  desires and aims and there may even be  some that see the undead is the future  in the likes of guinea we saw that he  actually relished living in the  hellscape and thus there might be other  characters who wish to infect people so  that they can rule there's definitely a  lot of possibilities and who knows the  need to eat may even have proven too  much for namra she does look somewhat  healed in this final scene and therefore  it is possible that she could have eaten  beyond this though she might have found  a way to consume normal food and be  sustaining herself of this namra in the  end very much represents what the  teacher wanted his son to be and in many  ways she is now a superhero she's very  much the end goal of the virus and has  likely found a way to heal without  having the insatiable hunger that is a  downside of being infected there's lots  of questions that could be answered in  the second season but with her and the  hybrids being carriers i still think  it's through them that the virus will  spread once more the characters did a  good job of keeping it contained in the  series but i'd love to see it  potentially even start to corrupt others  hell it might not even be the hybrids  that cause the issues and it could be  the humans that end up resenting those  that live in the restricted zones the  war very much divides the societies and  this may cause a divide in which the  regular humans wish to take back the  area and thus oust the hybrids it's  clear that the students don't want to  work with the uninfected as they've seen  that when push comes to shove they  completely disregard their lives  therefore they might even travel to the  other side and end up living with namra  and the other hybrids there's a lot of  things that could happen going forward  and as for my thoughts on the series  though i thought it was a little long at  points i did really enjoy it rocking in  at 12 hours makes it one of the longer  shows on netflix and there are certain  elements and scenes that i think could  have been cut to make it a better paced  show saying all that though once you're  in this world you really don't want to  leave it and the action acting and  character development are really well  done you feel for all these characters  and it's gripping watching the series  play out as you start to lose some of  your favorite people korea continues to  knock it out of the park when it comes  to shows and there's a lot going on in  this i'd love to see developed in a  second season all of us are dead was  great and it gets an 8.5 out of 10. now  i'd of course love to hear your thoughts  on the show so make sure you comment  below and let me know if you want  something else to watch then make sure  you check out our breakdown of hellbound  which will be linked on screen right now  that's another korean classic that's got  a supernatural element to it and if  you've seen the show then it's  definitely worth checking that one out  too without the way thanks for sitting  through the video i've been paul i'll  see you in the next one take care peace

